#: data/eu.jumplink.Steuererklaerung.metainfo.xml:7
msgid "Steuererklärung"
msgstr ""

#: data/eu.jumplink.Steuererklaerung.metainfo.xml:8
msgid "Taxes and bookkeeping"
msgstr ""

#: data/eu.jumplink.Steuererklaerung.metainfo.xml:10
msgid ""
"Receipts, transactions and invoices in one place. From them the app computes "
"the income-surplus statement (EÜR), the VAT returns, trade tax and the "
"separate assessment for partnerships, and files them through ELSTER."
msgstr ""

#: data/eu.jumplink.Steuererklaerung.metainfo.xml:11
msgid ""
"It runs on your machine: your bank data and documents stay in a local store. "
"Every figure can be traced back to the transaction it came from."
msgstr ""

#: data/eu.jumplink.Steuererklaerung.metainfo.xml:12
msgid ""
"AI is optional: everything works without it. If you want help from an AI "
"assistant, switch on the built-in MCP server and connect the assistant of "
"your choice. It can read your books and, only if you allow it, make changes."
msgstr ""

#: data/eu.jumplink.Steuererklaerung.metainfo.xml:13
msgid ""
"The tax logic follows German law, so the interface keeps the official German "
"terms."
msgstr ""

#: data/eu.jumplink.Steuererklaerung.metainfo.xml:14
msgid ""
"The app is an early version and a preparation aid, not tax advice: check "
"every return before you send it."
msgstr ""

#: data/eu.jumplink.Steuererklaerung.metainfo.xml:24
msgid "Overview with key figures and what to do next"
msgstr ""

#: data/eu.jumplink.Steuererklaerung.metainfo.xml:29
msgid "Receipts, linked to transactions"
msgstr ""

#: data/eu.jumplink.Steuererklaerung.metainfo.xml:34
msgid "All transactions of all accounts, searchable"
msgstr ""

#: data/eu.jumplink.Steuererklaerung.metainfo.xml:39
msgid "Outgoing invoices with status and recurring billing"
msgstr ""

#: data/eu.jumplink.Steuererklaerung.metainfo.xml:44
msgid "Anlage EÜR, every line down to its transactions"
msgstr ""

#: data/eu.jumplink.Steuererklaerung.metainfo.xml:49
msgid "Tax return with checks before filing"
msgstr ""

#: data/eu.jumplink.Steuererklaerung.metainfo.xml:60
msgid ""
"The macOS and Windows packages now include GTK, so the app starts without a "
"separately installed GTK. Empty totals no longer show a minus sign."
msgstr ""

#: data/eu.jumplink.Steuererklaerung.metainfo.xml:65
msgid ""
"The About dialog now links to the privacy policy and the legal notice. The "
"MCP server binds to loopback by default."
msgstr ""

#: data/eu.jumplink.Steuererklaerung.metainfo.xml:70
msgid ""
"The README now names which parts of the app are written with AI. The Flatpak "
"from Flathub comes without ERiC: export the return as XML and upload it in "
"Mein ELSTER."
msgstr ""

#: data/eu.jumplink.Steuererklaerung.metainfo.xml:75
msgid ""
"The Flatpak bundle on the GitHub release page includes ERiC, so validating "
"and submitting a return through ELSTER works from that download too."
msgstr ""

#: data/eu.jumplink.Steuererklaerung.metainfo.xml:80
msgid ""
"Restarting into the demo workspace works on macOS again, and the Flatpak "
"builds with the current assistant libraries. The AI assistant stays switched "
"off in this release."
msgstr ""

#: data/eu.jumplink.Steuererklaerung.metainfo.xml:85
msgid ""
"The AI assistant is optional and can be connected through the built-in MCP "
"server — every provider supported by Lotse can be used, and free hosted "
"models stay refused. The Linux packages ship their database libraries and "
"the Flatpak carries the demo workspace, so install and first run work out of "
"the box."
msgstr ""

#: data/eu.jumplink.Steuererklaerung.metainfo.xml:90
msgid ""
"Commands work in the installed app on Windows and macOS, Back up now no "
"longer opens a second window, and error messages follow the interface "
"language."
msgstr ""

#: data/eu.jumplink.Steuererklaerung.metainfo.xml:95
msgid ""
"First public release: receipts, transactions and invoices, the EÜR and VAT "
"returns, and filing through ELSTER."
msgstr ""

